    "description": "boot: board started (fw, reason, boot_id). command: a request was executed (op, ok, error, arg = ttl_ms / duration_us / edges). edge: a contact changed (state, cause). line: an undriven line changed level, or a driven line read high (level, state); polled every 10 ms; an undriven input that toggles by itself (floating) is no longer logged after 4 changes within 1-2 s, until it has been quiet for that long. config: mapping replaced (channels). wifi: network state (state). levels/driven are sampled when the event is recorded; for an edge that is right at the edge, before a released line has risen (the following line event shows the rise).",
    "properties": {
     "event": {
      "type": "string",
      "enum": [
       "boot",
       "command",
       "edge",
       "line",
       "config",
       "wifi"
